## Overview

**Civic-Flow** is a comprehensive civic engagement platform for Barangay Cubacub, Mandaue City, Cebu, Philippines. It provides a public-facing landing page, multi-step document request system, and six role-specific staff dashboards for barangay operations.

**Author:** Martin James Anog
**GitHub:** [@Develofer1](https://github.com/Develofer1)
**Contact:** martin.anog187@gmail.com

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 🏠 Public Landing Page | Community news, services, announcements |
| 📄 Document Request | 9 legal barangay documents, multi-step form |
| 📊 Finance Transparency | Public project tracker with budgets & milestones |
| 🏥 Clinic Handler | Patient queue, vaccination calendar |
| 📋 Document Handler | Request management, case history, verification |
| 🚨 Report Handler | Incident reports, case management, lost & found |
| 💰 Treasurer Dashboard | Project budget tracking, financial overview |
| 👑 Super Admin | Staff accounts, audit log, system settings |

---

## Tech Stack

- **Frontend:** React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Vite
- **UI Components:** Radix UI, shadcn/ui, MUI
- **Routing:** React Router v7
- **Backend (planned):** Django REST Framework
- **Database (planned):** PostgreSQL

---

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) v18 or higher
- [pnpm](https://pnpm.io) v8 or higher

### Installation

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/Develofer1/barangay-cubacub-civicflow.git
cd barangay-cubacub-civicflow

# 2. Install dependencies
pnpm install

# 3. Start the development server
pnpm run dev
```

Open your browser at **http://localhost:5173**

### Demo Login Credentials

| Role | Username | Password |
|---|---|---|
| Document Handler | `user1` | `pass1` |
| Report Handler | `user2` | `pass2` |
| Clinic Handler | `user3` | `pass3` |
| Treasurer | `treasurer` | `treas1` |
| Super Admin | `admin` | `admin` |

> ⚠️ These are demo credentials only. Change them before deploying.

---

## Available Scripts

```bash
pnpm run dev        # Start development server (http://localhost:5173)
pnpm run build      # Build for production (outputs to dist/)
pnpm run preview    # Preview the production build locally
```

